<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haakon IV of Norway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1204">1204</a>–<a href="/years/1263">1263</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Haakon Haakonsson, Haakon the Old</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haakon IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> reigned from 1217 and brought the long Norwegian civil wars to an end, defeating the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skule-bardsson">Skule Bårdsson</a> in 1240. His reign is seen as the height of medieval Norway. He drew Iceland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a> under the Norwegian crown in 1262–1264 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> after his campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> in 1263.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haakon-iv-of-norway.jpg" alt="Haakon IV of Norway" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drawing by Hakon Thorsen (d. before 1924) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kong_Haakon_Haakonsson_PI_III_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
